{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And all that they do.</b> Some say that he engaged in a craft from which to live, as the prisoners would do, but what is near to me is that its meaning is: all that they needed, as though he were the one doing it, for he was appointed over them. And the verse that comes after it is a witness."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:47:28.820384797Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}